---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusDashboard from '../components/StatusDashboard.astro';
---

<Layout title="Home" description="SpaceAge - Open PBEM Campaign Lobby">
  <section class="hero">
	<div class="hero-content">
	  <h1>SpaceAge Campaign</h1>
	  <p class="tagline">An Open Play-by-Email Galactic Strategy Game</p>

	  <p class="closed-lobby">
		This campaign is <strong>invitation-only</strong> — a closed table for ten player factions.
		There is no public sign-up; this site is for players and observers of that table.
	  </p>

	  <div class="attribution-block card" id="attribution">
		<h2>Lineage &amp; Attribution</h2>
		<p>
		  Original ideas are taken from <strong>Atlantis</strong> and <strong>Rise of Heroes</strong>,
		  and influenced by <strong>Vincent Archer</strong>. Archer wrote a 1998 generic PBEM engine
		  used by Overlord and then Rise of Heroes (1999–2000), intended for Atlantis-like games.
		  SpaceAge / Alderson sits in that family. SpaceAge is a <strong>spiritual successor</strong>,
		  not those games.
		</p>
		<p>
		  <a href="https://overlord.sourceforge.net/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Overlord PBEM engine (SourceForge)</a>
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="flavour">
		<h2>The Alderson Points</h2>
		<p class="flavour-lead">
		  A long, long time ago, in a galaxy far, far away… Or maybe in our future, here, in the Milky Way?
		</p>
		<p>
		  Alderson theorised <strong>weak points</strong> in space-time at the <strong>fringes of gravity wells</strong>.
		  From those points one could jump to another. The experimental <strong>Alderson Drive</strong> sent an expedition
		  more than <strong>750 light-years</strong> — and back the next week — in the wink of an eye. Today those Points
		  link the galaxy. Resources await explorers, traders, operators, and captains.
		</p>
		<p>
		  In a single day the Points <strong>shut down</strong>. Commerce died; colonies starved. After four months,
		  Points <strong>reopened</strong> — mostly the old links, some new. Contact never resumed with 10% of systems.
		  <strong>Two Points that led to Earth stayed dark.</strong> Radio from Sol dwindled to silence. Only the Fear remains.
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="pbem-intro card">
		<h3>How Play-by-Email Works</h3>
		<p>
		  You do not log into a live game. Instead, you read last quarter's report (text for now, visual tools later),
		  discuss strategy, and submit orders. When all factions are ready, the game engine processes the turn and
		  publishes new reports. The cycle repeats each quarter.
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="cta-buttons">
		<a href="/client" class="button">Open the Client</a>
		<a href="/turns" class="button button-secondary">View Turn Status</a>
	  </div>
	</div>

	<div class="hero-visual">
	  <div class="placeholder-visual">
		<p>★ Star Map Preview ★</p>
		<p style="font-size: 3rem; margin: 1rem 0;">✦</p>
		<p>Visual Tool Coming Soon</p>
	  </div>
	</div>
  </section>

  <section class="dashboard-section">
	<h2>Game Status</h2>
	<StatusDashboard />
  </section>

  <section class="features-section">
	<h2>Game Features</h2>
	<div class="features-grid">
	  <div class="card">
		<h3>Quarterly Turns</h3>
		<p>Each turn represents 13 weeks of in-game time. Strategy and diplomacy unfold across months of real time.</p>
	  </div>
	  <div class="card">
		<h3>Deep Technology Tree</h3>
		<p>Research and develop technologies across 10 levels, from basic fusion drives to advanced weapons and modules.</p>
	  </div>
	  <div class="card">
		<h3>Rich Simulation</h3>
		<p>Combat mechanics, resource management, crew skills, planetary environments, and diplomacy all affect your success.</p>
	  </div>
	</div>
  </section>

  <section class="rules-preview-section card">
	<h2>Quick Start</h2>
	<p>New to SpaceAge? Start with the <a href="/rules">rules overview</a> to understand the core mechanics.</p>
	<p>Want to dive deeper? Check out the <a href="/client">client page</a> for installation and getting started.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
	gap: var(--space-2xl);
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
	align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-content {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .hero h1 {
	font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
	margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .tagline {
	font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
	color: var(--color-accent-amber);
	font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
  }

  .closed-lobby {
	background-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12);
	border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-amber);
	padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
	border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .attribution-block h2 {
	margin-top: 0;
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
  }

  .flavour {
	background-color: rgba(13, 148, 136, 0.1);
	padding: var(--space-lg);
	border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-teal);
	border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .flavour h2 {
	margin-top: 0;
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
	font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
  }

  .flavour-lead {
	font-style: italic;
  }

  .pbem-intro {
	margin: var(--space-lg) 0;
  }

  .cta-buttons {
	display: flex;
	gap: var(--space-md);
	flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .button-secondary {
	background-color: var(--color-accent-blue);
  }

  .hero-visual {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
  }

  .placeholder-visual {
	background-color: rgba(13, 148, 136, 0.05);
	border: 2px solid var(--color-accent-teal);
	border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
	padding: var(--space-2xl);
	text-align: center;
	color: #666;
  }

  .dashboard-section {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .features-section {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .features-grid {
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
	gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .rules-preview-section {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
	.hero {
	  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
	}

	.cta-buttons {
	  flex-direction: column;
	}

	.button {
	  width: 100%;
	  text-align: center;
	}
  }
</style>
